3266\\t             (= 2 (count (:operands node)))\\n  3267\\t             (= :literal (:type (first (:operands node))))\\n  3268\\t             (contains? names (:value (first (:operands node)))))\\n  3269\\t      (u/app (u/v 'clj/define-global!)\\n  3270\\t             (u/lit (str (:value (first (:operands node)))))\\n  3271\\t             (publish-to-globals (second (:operands node)) names bound))\\n  3272\\t      (assoc node\\n  3273\\t             :operator (publish-to-globals (:operator node) names bound)\\n  3274\\t             :operands (mapv #(publish-to-globals % names bound)\\n  3275\\t                             (:operands node))))\\n  3276\\t    :if (cond-> node\\n  3277\\t          (contains? node :test)\\n  3278\\t          (assoc :test (publish-to-globals (:test node) names bound))\\n  3279\\t          (contains? node :consequent)\\n  3280\\t          (assoc :consequent (publish-to-globals (:consequent node) names bound))\\n  3281\\t          (contains? node :alternate)\\n  3282\\t          (assoc :alternate (publish-to-globals (:alternate node) names bound)))\\n  3283\\t    (reduce (fn [n k]\\n  3284\\t              (let [v (get n k)]\\n  3285\\t                (if (or (and (map? v) (contains? v :type)) (vector? v))\\n  3286\\t                  (assoc n k (globals-child v names bound))\\n  3287\\t                  n)))\\n  3288\\t            node (keys node))))\\n  3289\\t\\n  3290\\t\\n  3291\\t(defn lower-unit\\n  3292\\t  \\\"The `clj/run-main` entry's unit for the top-level source `forms`: one\\n  3293\\t   thunk whose call runs the program — `forms` plus the definitions of\\n  3294\\t   the guest library they need, compiled unmodified under `unit-opts`\\n  3295\\t   and published to the runtime global namespace by\\n2026-11-10 20:15:32 GMT\\n2026-11-11 03:15:32 +07\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-10 20:15:32 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 03:15:32 ICT\\n\\nReviewed `8cd9fc92..778747ce` statically. All line references below are at `778747ce`. No files edited; no suites rerun.\\n\\n1. **P1 must-fix — retained tokens are source-readable and transferable.**  \\n   `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1546` inserts the compiler token into the map subsequently bound directly to the catch variable at `:1142`. The public escape at `:1314` authenticates only that token, without binding it to the original condition.\\n\\n   After catching a genuine condition, source can throw an unrelated map:\\n   ```clojure\\n   (throw {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/unsupported-binding\\n           :yang.call/data {:forged true}\\n           :dsg__condition (:dsg__condition e)})\\n   ```\\n   It passes authentication and escapes as a protocol condition rather than a fresh thrown payload. Reserved-symbol checks do not prohibit this keyword lookup. Token equality therefore fixes literal-`true` forgery but does **not** satisfy R5.\\n\\n   **Disposition:** bind provenance to the retained condition through an opaque association or a witness authenticating its complete contents. Add token-transplant and modified-condition regressions.\\n\\n2. **P1 must-fix — ordinary caught exceptions now expose the envelope instead of the original exception.**  \\n   `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1536` includes `:yang.call/thrown` in the whole-condition retention branch at `:1545`. Catch lowering still exposes that whole map (`:1142`), while `rewrite-ex-info` still implements exception accessors as direct `:yin.k/message`/`:yin.k/data` lookups (`:915`).\\n\\n   Consequently, this public-call path statically yields `[nil nil]` instead of `[\\\"boom\\\" {:x 1}]`:\\n   ```clojure\\n   (let [f (fn [] (throw (ex-info \\\"boom\\\" {:x 1})))]\\n     (try (f)\\n          (catch Exception e [(ex-message e) (ex-data e)])))\\n   ```\\n   Direct intra-unit throws still expose the original payload, making ordinary catch behavior depend on routing. Whole-condition retention is necessary; changing the source-visible exception is not required by R3.\\n\\n   **Disposition:** preserve the original exception’s catching/accessor behavior while retaining the complete wire condition privately. Add a dynamic-call catch regression alongside the existing direct-throw tests.\\n\\n3. **P1 must-fix — retention can delete an original condition field.**  \\n   `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1546` overwrites any incoming `:dsg__condition` field. Both outbound strippers (`:1318`, `:2444`) then remove it. A genuinely transferred protocol condition containing that field as ordinary data therefore cannot be forwarded unchanged—even without source modification.\\n\\n   **Disposition:** store provenance outside the original condition, retaining the complete original map. Add a boundary fixture containing `:dsg__condition :ordinary-evidence` and assert exact preservation after immediate and saved rethrow.\\n\\n4. **P2 should-fix — two updated value-path assertions do not pin the required outer contract.**  \\n   `test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2620` and `:2637` inspect only the nested `:yang.call/not-callable` reason. Neither checks the outer `:yang.call/thrown` reason or callee evidence; the tail assertion also lacks an explicit error-tag check.\\n\\n   **Disposition:** assert the outer reason, error tag, inner reason, and callee evidence. The other three changed refusal expectations (`:2599`, `:2738`, `:2769`) already compare complete expected outcomes. All five wrapping changes are justified by ruling `1794332020000`; the concern is incomplete assertions, not the decision to wrap.\\n\\nThe six review questions resolve as follows:\\n\\n| Question | Assessment |\\n|---|---|\\n| **1. R3 retention** | **Not clean:** original-field loss in finding 3. Ordinary marker-free protocol conditions follow the intended immediate/saved rethrow path; no additional double-transfer or after-call fallthrough found in the changed bridge. |\\n| **2. Provenance** | **Not clean:** finding 1. Mechanically, all six writers stamp `dsg__call_token`, and both readers use token equality; no truthiness reader remains. |\\n| **3. Top-outcome guard** | **Clean structurally:** vector/count checks precede indexing. Descriptor maps pass through. Ordinary guest two-vectors are inside successful outcomes and are not mistaken for the outer error outcome. Provenance remains subject to finding 1. |\\n| **4. Ordinary behavior/tests** | **Not clean:** finding 2 and assertion gap 4. Remaining large churn is indentation, plus the documented retention, stripping, and tail changes. |\\n| **5. Tail semantics** | **Clean statically:** `tails/remark-tails` runs at `:2685`, after all outcome wrappers and before annotation. No new path skips re-marking where the stripper is installed. |\\n| **6. Scope** | **Clean:** exactly the two authorized files and two specified commits. |\\n\\nREQUEST CHANGES\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":941098,\"cached_input_tokens\":846336,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":4691,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":1621}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
