{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-10 22:58:05 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 05:58:05 ICT\n\nReviewed `778747ce..c9c5533c` read-only. Reproduced the failures below on **both walker and semantic lanes** at `c9c5533c`. Three focused existing tests passed: **28 assertions, 0 failures/errors**.\n\n| Finding | Verdict | Location |\n|---|---|---|\n| P1-1: transplant/provenance | **STILL BROKEN — P1**: complete contents can be transplanted between cells; retention is not bound to wrapper identity. | [clojure.cljc:972](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:972) |\n| P1-2: ordinary catch behavior | **STILL BROKEN — P1**: direct accessors/equality work, but other observations expose the wrapper and violate payload identity. | [clojure.cljc:1911](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1911) |\n| P1-3: original condition field deletion | **CONFIRMED FIXED**: the original condition is stored and forwarded without stamping or stripping fields. | [clojure.cljc:1664](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1664), [clojure.cljc:1438](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1438) |\n| P2-4: incomplete outer-contract assertions | **CONFIRMED FIXED**: assertions now cover error tags, outer thrown reasons, inner refusal reasons, and callee evidence. | [clojure_test.clj:2845](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2845), [clojure_test.clj:2866](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2866) |\n\n**Cell-forgery ruling:** arbitrary forged contents fail witness comparison, but complete-content replay succeeds. Consequently, the mechanism is insufficient for the required identity-owned lifetime association.\n\n`cell/authentic?` checks a live heap ID and its allocated seal; it does **not** certify compiler allocation or immutable contents ([engine.cljc:332](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:332)). Guests can allocate authentic cells, read contents, and replace contents through the exported cell operations ([engine.cljc:2773](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2773)).\n\nThe opaque witness closure prevents constructing a matching witness for different visible/condition values: closure equality compares owner and payload ([values.cljc:43](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc:43); [data.cljc:484](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:484)). However, neither the witness nor its comparison binds the cell ID.\n\nBoth lanes accepted:\n\n```clojure\n(throw (cell/new (cell/get e)))\n```\n\nThis forwarded the original protocol condition from a **new guest-created cell**. More decisively, after catching another genuine exception:\n\n```clojure\n(cell/set! e (cell/get other))\n(throw e)\n```\n\nThe same original wrapper now forwarded the **other condition**. My probe replaced the original `:yang.call/not-callable` condition with `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown :yang.call/value :replacement}`.\n\n**No guest-applied callable:** the decoder does not invoke the supplied proof; it type-checks and compares it against a compiler-generated closure. That part passes. The stronger requirement that decoding read only compiler-controlled state fails: the decoded heap contents are guest-readable and guest-writable.\n\n**Identity and observation:** the following results were identical on both lanes. Here `e` catches a dynamically thrown `orig = {:a 1}`, except where stated.\n\n| Observation | Actual | Required payload behavior |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `(= e orig)` | `true` | `true` |\n| `(= [e] [orig])` | `false` | `true` |\n| `(get {orig :found} e :missing)` | `:missing` | `:found` |\n| `(count e)` | `3` | `1` |\n| `(get (assoc e :a 2) :a)` | `1` | `2` |\n| Caught `nil`: `(if e :truthy :falsey)` | `:truthy` | `:falsey` |\n| Caught vector: direct `(vector? e)` versus aliased `(p e)` | `[true false]` | `[true true]` |\n\nThus, **not every guest observation answers the payload**. The predicate rewrite depends on the call’s spelling ([clojure.cljc:1279](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-r3-orch/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1279)); equality normalization is shallow; lookup does not normalize its key; truth tests remain unchanged.\n\n`assoc` does not modify the retained heap condition, so adding forged reason/data fields does not forge a new protocol condition. But leaving it unrouted is **not semantically safe**: ordinary payload updates disappear, as demonstrated above. `cell/set!` separately permits replacing what gets forwarded.\n\nThe witness prevents independently changing either authenticated slot while retaining the old proof. Nevertheless, observations diverge between payload and wrapper, and complete-content replacement changes the condition associated with an existing wrapper. Unmodified rethrow works only while that exposed association remains intact.\n\n**Test integrity:** no previously passing expectation was weakened or moved in `db2434dd`. Comparing reader forms after normalizing generated symbols and regex literals found only two changed existing forms: `av-modules` adds cell registration, and `test-value-invocation-refusals-are-terminating` strengthens assertions. The `defn` reflow adds no semantic change. The new tests miss the replay, mutation, nested-identity, and indirect-observation cases above.\n\n**CHANGES STILL REQUIRED**"}}
